"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"System is a fundomental part of ECS paradigm.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Use systems to implement any behavior or logic that updates entities every frame,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"such as different types of objects or characters. For example, a physics simulation system calculates and applies the affect of gravity, forces, and collisions for all entities.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A complex game or experience may consist of many systems which need to be executed in a specific order.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"The dependencies property defines when the update method for each system is called each frame. Update order is defined between system types and not between individual system instances.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Like example, let’s create a movement system:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["@PlainSystem","struct MovementSystem {","","    \/\/ Configure the query to world.","    \/\/ We want to recieve entities with `PlayerComponent` and `Transform`","    @FilterQuery<Ref<Transform>, With<PlayerComponent>>","    private var query","","    @Res<Input>","    private var input","","    init(world: World) {}","","    func update(context: UpdateContext) {","        self.query.forEach { transform in","            if input.isKeyPressed(.space) {","                \/\/ Add 5 points for vertical direction","                \/\/ if space button pressed","                transform.position.y += 5","            }","        }","    }","}",""],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"System","kind":"identifier"}],"externalID":"s:6AdaECS6SystemP","module